* models.lib - behavioural models for the quartz / LCD pickup head simulation
* Plain SPICE (G, E, R, C, D, V): runs in ngspice, LTspice and KiCad's simulator.
*
* Op amp macromodel: transconductance into a single dominant pole, output clamped near the
* rails by diodes, resistive output.  Pins: in+ in- out vcc vee.
*   GBW = gm / (2*pi*Cp), A0 = gm*Rp.  Noise sources (VN, IN) are 0 V / 0 A here; the noise
*   analysis drives them from Python.  Real parts have more poles: this model says nothing
*   about phase margin.

* ---- TI TLV9062: GBW 10 MHz, Aol ~110 dB, Ib 0.5 pA, Cin cm 4 pF / diff 2 pF
.subckt TLV9062 inp inn out vcc vee
VN  inp inpi 0
CCMP inpi 0 4p
CCMN inn 0 4p
CDIF inpi inn 2p
EMID mid 0 vcc vee 0.5
G1  0 n1 inpi inn 1m
RP  n1 mid 316.2Meg
CP  n1 mid 15.915p
VHI vcc hi 0.65
VLO lo vee 0.65
DH  n1 hi DCLAMP
DL  lo n1 DCLAMP
EOUT oi 0 n1 0 1
RO  oi out 50
.ends TLV9062

* ---- TI OPA2376: GBW 5.5 MHz, Aol ~120 dB, Ib 0.2 pA
.subckt OPA2376 inp inn out vcc vee
VN  inp inpi 0
CCMP inpi 0 6p
CCMN inn 0 6p
CDIF inpi inn 13p
EMID mid 0 vcc vee 0.5
G1  0 n1 inpi inn 1m
RP  n1 mid 1G
CP  n1 mid 28.94p
VHI vcc hi 0.65
VLO lo vee 0.65
DH  n1 hi DCLAMP
DL  lo n1 DCLAMP
EOUT oi 0 n1 0 1
RO  oi out 50
.ends OPA2376

.model DCLAMP D(IS=1e-14 N=1)
* BAV199 low-leakage clamp diode (leakage of a few pA)
.model DBAV199 D(IS=2e-12 N=1.9)
